Package: arsbridge
Title: Convert Annotated TLF Shells and ADaM Spec to CDISC ARS JSON
Version: 0.1.0.9155
Authors@R:
    person("Hamid", "Tavakoli",
           email = "htavakoli@gmail.com",
           role  = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0574-7739"))
Description: Reads a lead programmer's already-annotated TLF shell, as
    either a Word document or an Excel workbook, together with the study's
    ADaM specification Excel, and produces a valid CDISC Analysis Results
    Standard (ARS) v1.0 ARM-TS JSON file suitable for consumption by
    'siera::readARS()'. An Excel shell can additionally be written back
    filled with the computed results, preserving the original layout, so
    the deliverable is the reviewed shell itself. Annotation extraction
    is style-agnostic: detects ADaM variable references whether marked by
    font colour, character formatting, brackets, or plain-text appended
    after the stub label. Deterministic parsing always runs and is a fully
    supported mode on its own. Where a shell needs more than regex can read,
    the preferred completion mechanism is an offline supplement: a reviewed
    JSON file, typically produced by a chat assistant inside a closed
    environment, supplied via 'supplement=' and applied with no API key and no
    network access. A live LLM reader ('ellmer'; Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, or
    an OpenAI-compatible provider such as GLM) is an optional convenience for
    sites that permit it, used only when no supplement is supplied and a
    provider key is configured. Every proposed variable, from either source,
    is gated against the ADaM specification, so an out-of-spec proposal is
    rejected and flagged rather than shipped.
